{
  "case_id": "2012-12-123",
  "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: I assume this is one of those difficult merits questions you were alluding to, it doesn't go to whether there's jurisdiction, but to whether the claim of a taking can be asserted by the partnership in question, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The closest case is Village of Norwood v. Baker."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Am I right in thinking that there is no dispute on that point, that the -- the takings claim could have been asserted by the Hornes, as producers, in the Court of Federal Claims?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They were held responsible because in their -- in their processing capacity, when they were doing the stemming, the seeding, the fumigating, the packing, that this was regarded by the Department of Agriculture as possession -- physical possession of the raisins and acquisition of the raisins, even though they never had title to the raisins."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0000-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They have no standing. They have no pocketbook injury. The -- the entire pocketbook injury in this case is borne by the Hornes in their capacity as a handler."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0000-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sections 14(a) and 15(a) of the AMAA. I don't think that's in dispute. So only producers are -- are regulated by this program. Only producers have a right to go through their remedies in the Department of Agriculture."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Okay, okay. So we shouldn't have to pay because this is all unconstitutional. And -- and now what's your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. McConnell",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is it has nothing to do with jurisdiction. Second, the Tucker Act does not apply to cases where -- where there is a defense being lodged to a monetary exaction. That's Apfel, as supplemented by Missouri Pacific Railroad."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What was the first? I forgot the first already. What was the first?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Palmore",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JOSEPH R. PALMORE ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Palmore",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "there are two problems with the raisin claim, a capacity problem and a just compensation problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Palmore",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, we think that -- for several reasons. First of all, the Apfel opinion that's referred to is just a plurality. It's not been adopted by the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: And you -- you think that's a close question? You think that the way the statute is supposed to operate, once it is held that this is an unconstitutional taking, is that every year, the government takes the raisins and every year, the grower goes to the Court of Claims and gets the money back for the raisins. Is that the program that Congress anticipated?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, of course, Congress didn't think this was a taking. And it -- and it built considerable administrative flexibility into the statute, and at the end of the day, that's what convinces us that Congress would not have intended to preclude compensation in the Court of Claims and to -- to opt for an injunction instead because the Secretary of Agriculture has wide latitude to adjust."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Agriculture",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Certainly, we have standing. When -- it's not third-party standing. All of the money comes out of our pocket, yes, we have standing. And secondly, we certainly -- and then that is in our capacity as handler. Essentially, the Department of Agriculture's view is that during those couple of days when the raisins are going through our packing plant, that we acquired them and possessed them during those couple of days and that we should have given them their -- their share. That's raisins, that's not money. But by the time they get around to enforcing that and so forth, the raisins are gone and now the money stands in -- stands in for the raisins. But that is a taking claim. We think it's a -- it's a straightforward taking claim under -- under Norwood and Missouri Pacific Railroad, that's a merits question. But in any event, it is not a problem of capacity. Whatever might be, that taking, that taking is in the capacity as a handler. Those are my two points."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-123",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "9a0a8804cdd0a2773e82090207a4e17ae62f4ecdc74e9c1e0075a5809e74db39",
      "evidence_id": "ev-9a0a8804cdd0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
